#====================================================================
# DRAFT - shared distributed fs: Errno 28 with free blocks means
#   inode exhaustion from concurrent heavy tasks; stagger builds
# 触发事件: gtk2 2.24.33 真机适配(2026-09-13),同池两台设备互相影响
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-shared-fs-inode-exhaustion
trigger_tool:           conan|make|cmake|python
phase:                  configuration|building|packaging
error_signature:        \[Errno 28\] No space left on device|
                        Errno 28.*mkdir|
                        can't create temporary file.*Read-only file system

severity:               2
category:               fs|ohos|environment|concurrency|diagnostics
match_keywords:         Errno 28, No space left on device, inode, distributed fs,
                        HMDFS, 共享存储, 并发任务, 错峰, df 空闲但写入失败,
                        stat -f, single package queue

title:                   Errno 28 with terabytes of free blocks means the shared distributed fs inode pool is exhausted by concurrent heavy tasks; diagnose with stat -f and stagger builds

root_cause: >-
  The /storage/Users distributed fs is shared across devices and sessions with
  one global inode pool. df shows hundreds of GB of free blocks while `stat -f`
  shows only thousands of free inodes. Concurrent heavy tasks (full Qt builds,
  10k-test suites, multiple conan-home caches) drain the pool; once free inodes
  drop below a few thousand, EVERY file creation from any task fails with
  Errno 28 regardless of block availability. A build dir also degrades after
  prolonged churn: creates start failing mid-build even in freshly made subdirs.
affected_scope:         All tasks on devices sharing the /storage/Users distributed fs. A single gtk2-scale build needs roughly 60-100k inodes for its configure/make tree; a qtdeclarative-scale build drains far more. Cleanup of finished job build trees releases inodes immediately.

verification_cmd:       stat -f /storage/Users/currentUser | grep Inodes; find <job>/conan-home -name "*.o" | wc -l

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           stagger-plus-clean-regenerable-build-dirs
rec_description: >
  Before launching a device build, check `stat -f ... | grep Inodes`: require
  at least 100k free for a gtk2-scale build. Clean only regenerable build
  artifacts of FINISHED jobs (their conan-home p/b build folders), never
  another session's sources or recipe data. Queue one package build at a
  time while the pool is under load (workflow: heavy tasks are staggered).
  Treat `df` block counts as meaningless for this failure class; Errno 28
  with free blocks always means inodes.
rec_command:            stat -f /storage/Users/currentUser | grep Inodes; rm -rf <finished-job>/conan-home/p/b/*
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               device-hygiene-procedure

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      wait-for-load-window
fallback_description:   If no cleanup is authorized, wait for the concurrent task to finish and re-probe inodes before relaunching.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          scheduling

forbid_1_pattern:       df.*.Avail.*high.*therefore.*not.*inode
forbid_1_reason:        Free blocks do not imply free inodes on this fs; the two are independent limits and inodes exhaust first under many-small-files workloads.
forbid_1_consequence:   Builds fail with Errno 28 despite "terabytes free" and the diagnosis is dismissed as impossible.

forbid_2_pattern:       rm -rf.*another.*(running|active).*job
forbid_2_reason:        Cleanup must only touch finished jobs' regenerable build dirs; another session's active task data is not ours to delete.
forbid_2_consequence:   Destroys a concurrent session's in-flight work.

principles:             P016
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

